882	     * the given {@code lastName} and {@code postcode}. The household is keyed on {@code (lastName,
883	     * postcode)}: the normalized last name and the postcode are hashed with SHA-256 and the leading
884	     * 12 hex characters of the digest form the identifier, so any two owners sharing a last name and
885	     * postcode — regardless of creation order or address — resolve to the same identifier
886	     * automatically. An owner without a postcode belongs to no shared household, so {@code null} is
887	     * returned.
