900	    /**
901	     * Builds the canonical household key that identifies the household a {@code lastName} and
902	     * {@code postcode} belong to: the normalized last name (case-insensitive, with collapsed
903	     * whitespace) joined to the postcode by {@code '|'}. This is the single definition of which
904	     * owner fields make up a household and how they are normalized;
905	     * {@link #householdIdFor(String, String)} hashes this key into the stored identifier, so any two
906	     * owners in the same household resolve to the same key and therefore the same identifier.
907	     *
908	     * @param lastName the household's last name
909	     * @param postcode the household's postcode
910	     * @return the normalized household key
